From: fil-c-utils maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Include signal.h before gzip's head macro on Fil-C AArch64

gzip 1.15 includes signal.h after gzip.h defines a legacy macro named head.
Pizfix's AArch64 signal context structs also have fields named head, so the
preprocessor corrupts those declarations. Include signal.h before the macro is
defined on the affected Fil-C target; the later include is then a guarded no-op.

--- a/gzip.c
+++ b/gzip.c
@@ -57,3 +57,6 @@ static char const license_msg[] =
 #include <config.h>
-
+#if defined __FILC__ && defined __aarch64__
+# include <signal.h>
+#endif
+
 #include "tailor.h"
